  "plan": {
    "version": "architectural-plan-1",
    "id": "saint-lucia-waterfront-courtyard-estate",
    "thesis": "A low, deeply shaded waterfront estate organized as a ceremonial arrival court, a tall central gallery, and a broad south-facing social belvedere. Two deliberately quieter suite wings frame the gallery, while the living, dining and terrace sequence opens toward the conceptual waterfront. Flat, stepped roof planes, limestone-toned private wings, ivory social volumes, bronze-framed openings and timber privacy screens create a contemporary Caribbean composition with substantial climatic shade and a memorable landward-to-water sequence.",
